{{Quote|They'll make a prison of Palmo before they're done. Mark my words.|translated=1|Lezine speaking in Ghor during a town hall on Ghorman|<ref name="Ever Been" />}}
'''Palmo''' was the [[capital]] [[city]] of the [[Colonies]] [[planet]] [[Ghorman]]. Often described as peaceful and elegant, buyers and [[fashion designer]]s from across the galaxy would visit the city to tour the showrooms, brokerages, and [[twillery|twilleries]] located there. Much like the rest of Ghorman,  the city suffered under the [[Imperial Era|reign]] of the [[Galactic Empire]], with [[Grand Moff]] [[Wilhuff Tarkin]] landing his [[cruiser]] on five hundred civilians in the [[Tarkin Massacre]] in [[19 BBY]]. With the city continuing to serve as the capital under the new Empire, the city became major hotspot of [[Ghorman Front|resistance]] as Imperial rule continued during the [[Suppression of Ghorman]]. When tensions on Ghorman reached a breaking point following the empire landing mining equipment to [[Gouge mining|gouge mine]] the planet for the rare mineral [[kalkite]], thousands of the city's residents descended onto [[Palmo Plaza]] in protest, only to be mowed down by [[Imperial Army|imperial troops]] in what became known as the [[Ghorman Massacre]]. By [[1 BBY]], Ghorman, along with Palmo, was considered virtually destroyed.

==Description==
{{Quote|All that gorgeous material gathered for display and sale in the capital city, Palmo. The perfect setting for buyers and designers from around the galaxy to tour the showrooms and brokerages of this peaceful and elegant metropolis.|Narrator of the "Welcome to Ghorman" video|audio=Palmo-OneYearLater.flac|<ref name="One Year Later" />}}
Palmo was the [[capital]] [[city]] of the [[planet]] [[Ghorman]].<ref name="One Year Later" /> It was situated between mountains and the sea with canals running around its borders and through its interior.<ref name="Ever Been AD">{{Andor|Ever Been to Ghorman?}} {{AD|Disney+}}</ref> Throughout the city, series of underground [[Spillway tunnels|tunnels]] were used by [[Twillery|twilleries]] in the production of [[Ghorman twill]].<ref name="Ever Been" />

==History==
{{Expandsect}}
===Producing Palmo===
{{Quote|Nineteen generations. One of the youngest twilleries in Palmo.|Enza Rylanz to Cassian Andor|<ref name="Friends Everywhere" />}}
[[File:HouseOfRylanzShowroom-FriendsEverywhere.jpg||thumb|left|250px|the House of Rylanz (pictured), a newer twillery in Palmo, was still over 19 generations old.]]

Long before the [[Imperial Era]], many [[Twillery|twilleries]],<ref name="Friends Everywhere" /> facilities that produced [[Ghorman twill]] from the [[Ghorman silk|silk]] produced by the native [[ghorlectipod]]s,<ref name="One Year Later" /> opened in Palmo. One such twillery, the [[House of Rylanz]], despite being over nineteen [[Reproduction|generations]] old, was considered one of the youngest twilleries in Palmo by the Imperial Era.<ref name="Friends Everywhere" /> As time passed, Ghorman twill became synonymous with luxury and quality, becoming a hot commodity [[The galaxy|galaxy]]-wide, and as such it rite of passage for fashion designers entering the industry to visit the planet. Adapting to the newfound fame, a planet-wide effort was put in place to transport Ghorman silk to Palmo.<ref name="One Year Later" /> New showrooms and brokerages opened along with the existing twilleries continuing to operate, allowing buyers to visit Palmo to purchase the valuable twill but also making the market quite competitive.<ref name="Friends Everywhere" /> Despite the competition, Palmo came to be known as a peaceful and elegant metropolis.<ref name="One Year Later" />

By the [[Republic Era|time]] of the [[Galactic Republic]],<ref name="One Year Later" /> Ghorman had joined the Republic,<ref name="Acolyte Visual Guide">''[[Star Wars: The Acolyte: The Visual Guide]]''</ref> with Palmo serving as the planetary capital of Ghorman.<ref name="One Year Later" /> Ghorman and its [[sector]], [[Sern sector|Sern]], was represented in the [[Galactic Senate]] by [[Bal-Cobor Sampurn]] during the [[High Republic Era]].<ref name="Acolyte Visual Guide" /> Even as the Republic began to decline, Ghorman continued to gain much political power due to valuable twill that was produced in Palmo.<ref name="One Year Later" />

===Procuring Palmo===
{{Main|Tarkin Massacre}}
{{Quote|It was Moff Tarkin. People wouldn't clear when he wanted to land&hellip; and more of us kept coming. We thought there was safety in numbers. Who would land a cruiser on a crowd full of unarmed citizens?|Thela, to Cassian Andor|<ref name="Friends Everywhere" />}}
[[File:MonumentOfTheFallen-EverBeenToGorman.jpg||thumb|right|250px|the Monument to the Fallen (pictured), was erected in memory of those killed during the Tarkin Massacre]]
Even as the Republic continued to decline, the [[Ghorman (people)|people]] of Ghorman stayed loyal to the Republic, with the role of the sector's [[senator]] eventually falling on [[Fang Zar]] by [[19 BBY]]. That same year, [[Supreme Chancellor]] [[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine]] declared himself [[Galactic Emperor]], and reformed the Republic into the [[Galactic Empire]] with the promise of a safe and secure society. However, the residents of the planet, not wanting to be a part of the new empire, took to the streets of Palmo in peaceful demonstrations of the Empire. In response, Imperial [[Moff]] [[Wilhuff Tarkin]] was dispatched to the [[Ghorman system]], and upon his arrival, ordered his [[cruiser]] to land on the demonstrators at [[Palmo Plaza]]. In the resulting slaughter, five hundred unarmed protesters were crushed to [[death]] in what became known as the [[Tarkin Massacre]]. Soon after the massacre, a [[Monument to the Fallen|memorial monument]] was constructed at the site of the massacre.<ref name="Friends Everywhere" /> Due to Ghorman's political power, the Galactic Empire was pressured into maintaining only small presence on the Ghorman,<ref name="One Year Later" /> mainly leaving only service branches such as the [[Imperial Bureau of Standards]] to continue operations on the planet from an [[Imperial office complex|office complex]] just off Palmo's capital square. Despite the low presence, the effects of Imperial rule could still be felt, and as a result a resistance movement known as the [[Ghorman Front]] began to take shape in Palmo.<ref name="Ever Been" />

===Provoking Palmo===
{{Expandsect}}
{{Main|Suppression of Ghorman}}
By [[5 BBY]], [[Tarkin Initiative]] scientists developing the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station]]'s [[Mk I Superlaser]] as part of [[Project Celestial Power]] discovered the need for the [[mineral]] [[Kalkite]] for use in [[reactor]] lens coatings. The only known deposits of the rare mineral were on Ghorman, and as such [[Director of Advanced Weapons Research]] [[Orson Callan Krennic|Orson Krennic]] began making preparations for mining Ghorman. At a [[Maltheen Divide conference|secret conference]] at the [[Maltheen Divide]] in [[4 BBY]], Imperial officials planned the [[suppression of Ghorman]],<ref name="One Year Later" /> with [[ISB Supervisor]] [[Dedra Meero]] subsequently being placed in charge of the [[Ghorman project|project]]. With the intention of radicalizing resistance to justify a military takeover and allow mining, Meero, now the acting [[governor]] of the planet, established her base of operations at the Imperial Office Complex just off Palmo Plaza.<ref name="WAY" /> Simultaneously, in preparation for a military takeover, the Empire began building an [[Palmo armory|armory]] in Palmo under the cover of being a "new office complex."<ref name="Friends Everywhere" />

{{stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Palmo appeared in the [[Andor Season 2|second season]] of the live-action series ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]'', first being mentioned in the season's first episode, "[[One Year Later]]," which was released on [[Disney+]]<ref name="One Year Later" /> on [[April 22]], [[2025]]<ref name="Trailer News">{{SW|url=news/andor-season-2-teaser-trailer-key-art-reveal|text=First ''Andor A Star Wars Story'' Teaser Trailer and Poster Revealed}}</ref> and later first being shown in the season's fourth episode, "[[Ever Been to Ghorman?]]",<ref name="Ever Been" /> released on [[April 29]], [[2025]].<ref name="Trailer News" />

